    const-string v3, "What happened: a Linux process inside the container hit a native error (often while the phone was under memory pressure). This is not a normal force-stop by PocketLinux.\n\nSuggestions (optional \u2014 you stay in control):\n\u2022 Close other Android apps to free RAM, then start the desktop again.\n\u2022 On Android 12+: Developer options \u2192 turn on \u201cDisable child process restrictions\u201d so Linux child processes are less likely to be killed.\n\u2022 Set PocketLinux battery use to Unrestricted if the session dies in the background.\n\u2022 Keep notifications allowed so the \u201csession running\u201d notice can help Android leave the session alone."

